# ============================================================================
# MarketPulse — .gitignore
# This file lists everything git should PRETEND DOESN'T EXIST.
# Think of it as the bouncer outside the git club: the names on this list
# never get past the velvet rope into a commit.
# ============================================================================

# --- The most important lines in this file ---------------------------------
# learning/ — my private "teach-me-this-tech" notes. Interview prep, not
# production. Never goes on a public repo.
learning/

# .claude/ — local planning / scratch notes for this project's master plan.
# Stays on my disk; never pushed.
.claude/

# docs/ — my personal command journal + scratch design notes. Private.
# (If I ever write a public-facing architecture.md or ADR I'll un-ignore it
# selectively with `!docs/architecture.md` etc.)
docs/

# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# .env files hold API keys (Alpaca, Groq, HuggingFace, AWS). Leaking these
# into git is a career-ending mistake. If you ever accidentally commit a
# secret, ROTATE it on the provider — don't just delete the file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
dist/
build/

# --- uv ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# uv.lock IS committed (so everyone gets reproducible installs)
# but caches and downloaded wheels are not
.uv-cache/

# --- Tests / coverage -------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Notebooks --------------------------------------------------------------
# Strip outputs before committing notebooks — outputs balloon repo size
# and often contain secrets in cells we forgot to clear.
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Data / models / artifacts ---------------------------------------------
# Everything large enough to need DVC/S3 instead of git.
# IMPORTANT: leading slash makes these root-only — otherwise `data/` would
# match the Python package `services/forecast/src/forecast/data/` too.
/data/
*.parquet
*.csv
/models/
/checkpoints/
/mlruns/
/lightning_logs/        # Lightning Trainer dumps hparams.yaml + version_N/ here
/wandb/
*.pt
*.pth
*.bin
*.ckpt
*.safetensors

# --- Docker -----------------------------------------------------------------
# nothing to ignore for docker itself, but compose may write these
.docker/

# --- Frontend (Next.js) ----------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
out/
.vercel/

# --- IDE / OS ---------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# --- Local logs -------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
